import{_ as o,o as i,c as t,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 724 | Transcended-Ones' Perpetual-Construction System | More-Work-More-Gain Allocation of Perpetual Construction","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 724 | Transcended-Ones' Perpetual-Construction System | More-Work-More-Gain Allocation of Perpetual Construction","no":724,"module":4,"tags":["Perpetual Construction","More-Work-More-Gain","Joint Contracting","Civilizational-Weight Allocation","Contribution Quantification"],"related":["06-More-Work-More-Gain Allocation Principle","22-Resource-Allocation Joint-Contracting Mechanism","25-Symbiotic Feedback-Cycle Mechanism"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0724_模块4-永动建设的多劳多得分配.md","filePath":"en/0724_模块4-永动建设的多劳多得分配.md"}`),a={name:"en/0724_模块4-永动建设的多劳多得分配.md"};function r(s,e,l,c,h,u){return i(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n(`<h1 id="entry-724-transcended-ones-perpetual-construction-system-more-work-more-gain-allocation-of-perpetual-construction" tabindex="-1">Entry 724 | Transcended-Ones&#39; Perpetual-Construction System | More-Work-More-Gain Allocation of Perpetual Construction <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-724-transcended-ones-perpetual-construction-system-more-work-more-gain-allocation-of-perpetual-construction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 724 | Transcended-Ones&#39; Perpetual-Construction System | More-Work-More-Gain Allocation of Perpetual Construction&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 06, 22, 25</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-work-is-not-asceticism-it-is-positive-feedback" tabindex="-1">Introduction: work is not asceticism, it is positive feedback <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-work-is-not-asceticism-it-is-positive-feedback" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: work is not asceticism, it is positive feedback&quot;">​</a></h2><p>If perpetual construction has only the pressure of &quot;you must work&quot; without the feedback of &quot;working pays off,&quot; it becomes hard labor, unsustainable for a million years. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s solution is <strong>more-work-more-gain</strong> — the more you work, the larger the public computable power you may dispatch; the larger your output, the higher your civilizational weight; the higher your weight, the larger the civilizational engineering you may take on. This is a positive feedback, not a punishment.</p><p>Six top-level axioms in this entry converge into the word &quot;allocation&quot;: the anti-predation axiom requires allocation by contribution only, not by predation; the republican axiom of Myriad Races requires allocation rules be equal to all beings; the collective ascension axiom requires allocation serve the uplift direction; the causal self-discipline axiom requires allocation processes be transparent and auditable; the law-first axiom requires allocation algorithms be stable, not adjusted by plot needs.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-the-core-of-allocation-civilizational-weight-is-the-allocation-voucher" tabindex="-1">I. The Core of Allocation: Civilizational Weight Is the Allocation Voucher <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-the-core-of-allocation-civilizational-weight-is-the-allocation-voucher" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. The Core of Allocation: Civilizational Weight Is the Allocation Voucher&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s allocation is not &quot;paying wages,&quot; but <strong>civilizational weight as allocation voucher</strong>.</p><ul><li>The higher your civilizational weight, the larger your share in the joint-contracting resource pool;</li><li>The higher your civilizational weight, the larger the law-weaving engineering you may participate in;</li><li>The higher your civilizational weight, the larger your voice in the Myriad-Rank Republican Council;</li><li>The higher your civilizational weight, the more cross-plane-channel quotas you may dispatch.</li></ul><p>This means: <strong>allocation is not &quot;rewarding your past contribution,&quot; but &quot;giving you a larger stage to keep contributing.&quot;</strong> Your weight is high not because you may enjoy, but because Myriad Ranks trust you to take on larger engineering.</p><h2 id="ii-three-quantitative-dimensions-of-more-work-more-gain" tabindex="-1">II. Three Quantitative Dimensions of More-Work-More-Gain <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-three-quantitative-dimensions-of-more-work-more-gain" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Three Quantitative Dimensions of More-Work-More-Gain&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Per Documents 06 and 22, more-work-more-gain at the transcended-one level is concretely quantified in three dimensions:</p><h3 id="_2-1-hours-dimension" tabindex="-1">2.1 Hours Dimension <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-1-hours-dimension" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.1 Hours Dimension&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The time and energy a transcended one actually invests on post. This is not &quot;clocking in,&quot; but effective hours — how many anchors you actually calibrated on the Maintenance Post; how many latecomers you actually guided on the Guidance Post; how many new manuals you actually developed on the Increment Post.</p><h3 id="_2-2-output-dimension" tabindex="-1">2.2 Output Dimension <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-2-output-dimension" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.2 Output Dimension&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The efficiency with which hours convert into civilizational increments. Given the same hours, how many cultivators use the new manuals you developed; how many of the latecomers you guided pass four-dimensional assessment; how many planes onboard the new laws you wove. The output dimension matters more than the hours dimension — it measures &quot;effective contribution.&quot;</p><h3 id="_2-3-coverage-dimension" tabindex="-1">2.3 Coverage Dimension <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-3-coverage-dimension" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.3 Coverage Dimension&quot;">​</a></h3><p>How many clans, how many planes, how many life forms your work benefits. A transcended one serving only humankind naturally has a lower coverage dimension than one serving Myriad Ranks. This encourages transcended ones structurally to expand work toward 99% of clans.</p><p>The three dimensions are weighted to yield this transcended one&#39;s current-period civilizational-weight increment. Increments accumulated are his total weight.</p><h2 id="iii-allocation-s-anti-matthew-principle" tabindex="-1">III. Allocation&#39;s Anti-Matthew Principle <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-allocation-s-anti-matthew-principle" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Allocation&#39;s Anti-Matthew Principle&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The old world&#39;s allocation is often Matthew-effect: the rich get richer; the poor get poorer. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s more-work-more-gain has a key correction — <strong>anti-Matthew principle</strong>:</p><ul><li>For latecomers: basic cultivation resources are prioritized, not monopolized by &quot;arrivistes&quot;;</li><li>For transcended ones: high weight brings not &quot;private-property accumulation,&quot; but &quot;larger public responsibility&quot;;</li><li>For Myriad Ranks: the resource pool&#39;s total flow keeps expanding because of the Increment Post; it is not zero-sum.</li></ul><p>This means: <strong>your weight is high not because you &quot;save more&quot;; your weight is high because you &quot;spend more on public engineering.&quot;</strong> Civilizational weight may not be exchanged for private enjoyment; it may only be invested in the next round of construction.</p><h2 id="iv-the-meshing-of-allocation-with-the-perpetual-cycle" tabindex="-1">IV. The Meshing of Allocation with the Perpetual Cycle <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-the-meshing-of-allocation-with-the-perpetual-cycle" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. The Meshing of Allocation with the Perpetual Cycle&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The more-work-more-gain allocation mechanism is the gear of perpetual construction&#39;s positive-feedback cycle (see Entry 721):</p><div class="language- vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span>work more → civilizational weight rises → larger public computable power to dispatch</span></span>
<span class="line"><span> ↑                                                         ↓</span></span>
<span class="line"><span> ←─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Without the allocation mechanism, this cycle cannot spin — you work half a day, computable power does not grow, next time you start from scratch. With the allocation mechanism, every time you work, your next work starts from a higher point. This is the mechanism foundation at the allocation level of &quot;the more you work, the stronger you get.&quot;</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: more-work-more-gain lets cultivators who maximize effective contribution get the largest computable power, preventing &quot;muddling along and occupying resources&quot;</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: allocation is by contribution only, not by predation — predatory-faction strong ones get no high weight in this algorithm</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-style allocation is &quot;the protagonist takes the lion&#39;s share, disciples drink soup&quot;; Heng Yuan Zhou-style allocation is &quot;keep ledgers by contribution, divide stages by weight&quot;</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the coverage dimension explicitly includes service to 99% of clans in allocation computation</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: allocation algorithms, weight ledgers, historical records are all public in the Selfless-Dao public library</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>More-work-more-gain is not a slogan; it is perpetual construction&#39;s allocation engine. It makes the transcended one feel, every time he works, &quot;this time I have more drive than last&quot;; it lets Myriad Ranks see that the larger the contributor&#39;s contribution, the larger his stage — not the more he enjoys.</p><p>This mechanism also has a social function often overlooked: it makes &quot;being strong&quot; no longer envied, but expected. In the old world, after a person becomes strong, those around him are instinctively wary — is he going to exploit us? Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s more-work-more-gain allocation lets those around see: he became strong, his stage grew, his work grew, the civilizational fruits we enjoy also grew. Strength is no longer a threat; strength is an amplifier of public interest. <strong>This is Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s strong-one ethics: not making you poorer the more you work, but making you more able to keep working the more you work.</strong></p><p>In the end, the more-work-more-gain allocation of perpetual construction described in this entry is no isolated case — its causal and energetic traces are throughout filed in the Alaya Network, traceable and correctable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/06-多劳多得分配原理.html">Entry 06 · More-Work-More-Gain Allocation Principle</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/22-资源分配联产承包机制.html">Entry 22 · Resource-Allocation Joint-Contracting Mechanism</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/25-共生反馈循环机制.html">Entry 25 · Symbiotic Feedback-Cycle Mechanism</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/65-能量标准化与计量.html">Entry 65 · Energy Standardization and Measurement</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>`,35)])])}const m=o(a,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
